{"skill":{"slug":"elevenlabs","displayName":"Elevenlabs"},"version":{"version":"1.3.4","createdAt":1772570407368,"changelog":"fix: use /Users/oliver/clawd for workspace root to preserve symlink paths","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SETUP.md","size":2977,"sha256":"47ad3800ef08de9cedc3584311e83acdfd67766a146132d7a2a108d993870845","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":5545,"sha256":"0315d0231c9940328770602de567706a9781bcc160bd0059b25d8b150189ea00","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/_pathguard.py","size":1869,"sha256":"2cadf9e671b1f0e736eb2e75231980de3b6bae02d542b16d0a5438c570f9b20e","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/dialogs.py","size":10724,"sha256":"c266245ad708b2fc8c836c8e58060e726430f754f218fdb925bb19765e1b33a8","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/music.py","size":4818,"sha256":"a3f92de8cb9f92fa97507f1a209eb6ec08dee55f4ff8891406f1d243db19f848","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/quota.py","size":10137,"sha256":"c406d9ec2fddb9b7a986ab5398d15a95e6d8b22eb9b4580b06f6b204fccd3b86","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/sfx.py","size":5244,"sha256":"f3942695f03786e8a86914e75851c8e462c8123f566f2b348e964b99552bfc76","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/speech.py","size":4381,"sha256":"a60dd314048766ab798d71e43fee503949b029a7ea08e9c960f46d2dd7675b14","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/voiceclone.py","size":8378,"sha256":"4bae054d9278a359d1d9a05823b32586498dd3ea48d38b87f0950111c3f9c982","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/voices.py","size":1666,"sha256":"6edd83708ea0e155d31a982c0deae80f9e8f4850c89a84cfeda16b467360f970","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2244,"sha256":"fc40a6ddc90bf9cf4b7e4ce72bf153f48216e577ed0a9fb17e56d6fa0e3ba99e","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789031397840,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"e17d3b1efa12b4fc22b63222f66403ff2bd247786870c8212004359e588fa198","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/e17d3b1efa12b4fc22b63222f66403ff2bd247786870c8212004359e588fa198","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: elevenlabs\nVersion: 1.3.4\n\nThe OpenClaw AgentSkills bundle for ElevenLabs is classified as benign. The skill demonstrates strong security practices, notably the `_pathguard.py` script which strictly limits output file writes to the workspace or `/tmp` directories, and the `voiceclone.py` script which restricts input audio file reads to a designated sample directory. All network requests are directed exclusively to the legitimate ElevenLabs API (api.elevenlabs.io). Command execution via `subprocess.run` (e.g., for `ffmpeg` and `afplay`) correctly uses a list of arguments, preventing shell injection. No evidence of prompt injection, data exfiltration, persistence mechanisms, or obfuscation was found in any of the files, including `SKILL.md` and `SETUP.md`.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779161153707},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":40,"checkedAt":1789031397840},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This ElevenLabs skill performs disclosed audio, voice, and quota operations against the ElevenLabs API, with sensitive voice-cloning behavior that users should handle carefully.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Network access, the ElevenLabs API key, local audio input, output file writes, ffmpeg, and optional afplay are proportionate for audio generation; output paths are guarded and voice-clone samples are restricted to an explicit sample directory unless the user overrides it.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Setup uses a normal pip install for requests and asks users to provide ELEVENLABS_API_KEY; the dependency is unpinned and shell-profile or .env persistence would store a reusable API key in plaintext.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Commands are user-invoked and scoped to named scripts, but the documentation should make voice-cloning consent and third-party data transmission more prominent and has minor feature mismatches around .env support, caching, and dialogue timestamps.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill may create or use ~/.openclaw/elevenlabs/voiceclone-samples and suggests persistent API-key configuration, but I found no cron jobs, startup hooks, background agents, privilege escalation, or hidden persistence.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The advertised purpose is ElevenLabs text-to-speech, sound effects, music, voice management, voice cloning, and quota checks; the scripts implement those functions against ElevenLabs API endpoints.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable sending text prompts, generation settings, account usage requests, and any selected voice samples to ElevenLabs. Use voice cloning only with recordings you own or have permission to use, protect the API key, prefer a virtual environment with pinned dependencies, and avoid storing the key in synced dotfiles or committed .env files.","findings":"[TT3] expected: The API key flows into xi-api-key headers for ElevenLabs API calls, which is expected authentication for this integration; I found no unrelated destination for the key.\n[E1] expected: External transmission of prompts, dialogue data, music settings, and audio samples is core to using ElevenLabs cloud APIs, not evidence of hidden exfiltration.\n[TP4] expected: Voice cloning is implemented and documented as a tool, though the top-level description uses the broader phrase voice management and should highlight cloning more clearly.\n[SQP-2] expected: The privacy concern is real guidance-wise, especially for voice samples, but the behavior is user-directed and coherent with an ElevenLabs API skill.\n[RA2] unexpected: The cited sample directory and state directory are disclosed local storage locations, not unauthorized session persistence or a background mechanism.\n[LP3] expected: The skill relies on shell-executed Python scripts, local files, environment credentials, and network API calls; a clearer least-privilege declaration would help but the authority matches the purpose.\n[SDI-4] unexpected: The dialogue documentation overstates timestamp and alignment support because the current endpoint handling returns audio only; this is a documentation accuracy issue, not malicious behavior.\n[AST4] expected: The subprocess uses are for ffmpeg splitting and optional afplay playback with argument lists rather than shell strings, which is purpose-aligned.\n[T08] unexpected: Installing requests without a pinned version is a supply-chain hardening gap, not evidence that the skill itself is malicious.\n[T09] unexpected: Several requests calls lack explicit timeouts, creating an availability risk if a network operation stalls; this does not add persistence, exfiltration, or privilege escalation.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789031397840}}}}}